  "simulation_id": "zoom_return_to_office_10actor",
  "title": "Zoom's Return-to-Office Mandate",
  "objective": "Simulate the tensions and negotiations around Zoom's 2023 return-to-office policy, balancing productivity, real estate commitments, and talent retention.",
  "brief": "Zoom's return-to-office mandate (2023). The company that became synonymous with remote work told employees living within 50 miles to come to the office at least twice a week. Stakeholders: a deaf employee who thrives with remote async communication and whose productivity dropped 40% in open-plan offices, an engineering manager who believes in-person whiteboard sessions produce better architecture decisions, Zoom's commercial real estate lease negotiator who secured long-term office leases pre-pandemic, and a competitor (Microsoft Teams) enterprise sales director spotting a recruiting opportunity among disgruntled Zoom employees.",
